From 8d5559eb225b359c73cfd69cb21fec500668912f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: proshiv85-byte <proshiv85@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 23:32:11 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 11/16] WIP: Exynos8895 CPU idle (core power-down)

PSCI CPU_SUSPEND idle state per cluster, values from the vendor kernel.
The firmware only prepares the core; exynos8895-cpupm programs the
core's local power configuration in the PMU around the PSCI call
(CPU PM notifier), like the vendor exynos_cpu_pm_enter/exit. Cluster
power-down is disarmed at boot: the bootloader leaves it enabled on the
Mongoose cluster, and with a core-only PSCI state the L2 lost its dirty
lines once all four cores were off (memory corruption).

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic)
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos8895.dtsi |  31 +++++
 drivers/soc/samsung/Kconfig                |  11 ++
 drivers/soc/samsung/Makefile               |   1 +
 drivers/soc/samsung/exynos8895-cpupm.c     | 125 +++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 168 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/soc/samsung/exynos8895-cpupm.c

